{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויגדל האיש וילך הלוך וגדל עד כי גדל", :translit "va-yigdal ha-ish va-yelech haloch va-gadal ad ki gadal", :gloss "and the man grew and went forward growing and growing until that he grew great"} {:he "שלשה גדולות", :translit "sheloshah gdolot", :gloss "three greatnesses"} {:he "כנגד ג' ברכות", :translit "keneged g' berachot", :gloss "corresponding to three blessings"} {:he "שנתברך בעקידה", :translit "she-nitbarech be-akeidah", :gloss "with which he was blessed at the Binding"} {:he "כי ברך אברכך", :translit "ki varach avarchecha", :gloss "for I will surely bless you"} {:he "והתברכו בזרעך", :translit "ve-hitbarechu ve-zar'echa", :gloss "and all the nations of the earth shall bless themselves by your seed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Threefold repetition of root ג-ד-ל in the verse corresponds to three blessings spoken at the Akeidah."}], :frame {:text "At the Akeidah, God says to Abraham: 'that in blessing I will bless you' (Genesis 22:17) and 'in your seed shall all the nations of the earth bless themselves' (Genesis 22:18). The phrase כי ברך אברכך uses infinitive absolute construction, which the Ba'al HaTurim reads as containing multiple blessings. The threefold repetition of the root ג-ד-ל in Genesis 26:13 (ויגדל, וגדל, גדל) signals that these blessings transfer to Isaac.", :sources ["Genesis 22:17" "Genesis 22:18" "Genesis 26:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Threefold repetition of root ג-ד-ל in the verse corresponds to three blessings spoken at the Akeidah.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:18.454485198Z", :model "glm-5.2"}